                <pb facs="0194" n="82" xml:id="pg82"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 23700/7.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to Minister Beaupré.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1910-03-31"><hi rendition="#italic">March 31,
                        1910</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Wilson informs Minister Beaupré that the extradition papers for Knepper,
                    referred to in legation’s telegram of March 31, will be sent on Saturday.</p>
            </div>
